IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voca-schedules`
IMPORT `voca-core`

-- Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2006 (NT) -- from the seat of THE VICTIM APPLYING FOR ASSISTANCE: a primary,
-- secondary, family or related victim of a violent act in the Northern Territory. "Is what happened to me a violent
-- act? What kind of victim am I, and what can I apply for? Does my motor accident or workers compensation cover it
-- instead? How much can I get, as an interim payment or an award? What reduces or bars it? When must I be paid, and
-- must I repay? Can I seek review?" Every question is phrased as that person asks it, on facts that person could state.
-- The rules are in voca-core.l4 and voca-schedules.l4; this module builds their records from plain answers and
-- restates no rule. Where an answer depends on an earlier question (whether the act is a violent act, its category,
-- whether ss 17-18 exclude me), the @desc says which question gives it.
--
-- Judgments the Act leaves to the Director or the assessor (financial hardship, "reasonable", the s 41 reduction, the
-- s 43 satisfactions, the reg 19 proportion) are asked as facts, so each answer is conditional on them.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Victims of crime assistance -- the victim's questions`

-- The offence, from plain answers (the Schedules' terms are in voca-schedules.l4).
GIVEN `the Criminal Code section of the offence` IS A STRING
      `it was an attempt`                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the offence`                    IS A DATE
      `the victim suffered serious harm`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `an offensive weapon was used or threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender was in the company of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `old s 188(2)(a) applied`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `old s 188(2)(c) applied`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `old s 188(2)(k) applied`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Schedule 2 condition for the offence applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how many related criminal acts there were`  IS A NUMBER
      `the acts happened over a period of time`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acts were all by the same offender against the same victim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Offence`
`the offence from my answers` `the Criminal Code section of the offence` `it was an attempt` `the date of the offence` `the victim suffered serious harm` `an offensive weapon was used or threatened` `the offender was in the company of another person` `old s 188(2)(a) applied` `old s 188(2)(c) applied` `old s 188(2)(k) applied` `the Schedule 2 condition for the offence applied` `how many related criminal acts there were` `the acts happened over a period of time` `the acts were all by the same offender against the same victim` MEANS
    `Offence` WITH
        `section`                                                        IS `the Criminal Code section of the offence`
        `was an attempt`                                                 IS `it was an attempt`
        `was committed before 25 March 2024`                             IS DATE_SERIAL `the date of the offence` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 25 3 2024)
        `was committed before 30 April 2023`                             IS DATE_SERIAL `the date of the offence` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 4 2023)
        `the victim suffered serious harm as a direct result`            IS `the victim suffered serious harm`
        `was committed by the use or threatened use of an offensive weapon` IS `an offensive weapon was used or threatened`
        `was committed by a person in the company of another person`     IS `the offender was in the company of another person`
        `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(a) applied`                    IS `old s 188(2)(a) applied`
        `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(c) applied`                    IS `old s 188(2)(c) applied`
        `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(k) applied`                    IS `old s 188(2)(k) applied`
        `the condition opposite it in Schedule 2 applied`                IS `the Schedule 2 condition for the offence applied`
        `how many related criminal acts the violent act is a series of`  IS `how many related criminal acts there were`
        `the related acts occurred over a period of time`                IS `the acts happened over a period of time`
        `the acts were committed against the same victim by the same offender` IS `the acts were all by the same offender against the same victim`

GIVEN `it happened in the Northern Territory`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it directly caused someone's injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence`                                IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A `Criminal act`
`the act from my answers` `it happened in the Northern Territory` `it was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` `it directly caused someone's injury or death` `the offence` MEANS
    `Criminal act` WITH
        `occurred in the Territory`                                        IS `it happened in the Northern Territory`
        `constitutes a criminal offence, or would but for an excuse in s 5(2)(b)` IS `it was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse`
        `directly resulted in the injury or death of one or more persons`  IS `it directly caused someone's injury or death`
        `the offence`                                                      IS `the offence`

-- One injury, as the victim describes it.
DECLARE `My injury` HAS
    `its Schedule 3 item`                                    IS A STRING
    `it is on both sides of my body, or to my only remaining one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the percent the assessor puts down to a condition I already had` IS A NUMBER
    `for scarring, it is permanent`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `for scarring, it was caused by burns I also claim for that part` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `mine` IS A LIST OF `My injury`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Injury claimed`
`my injuries as claimed` `mine` MEANS
    map (GIVEN `m` YIELD `Injury claimed` WITH
                            `Schedule 3 item`                               IS `m`'s `its Schedule 3 item`
                            `on each side of the body`                      IS `m`'s `it is on both sides of my body, or to my only remaining one`
                            `percent attributable to an existing condition` IS `m`'s `the percent the assessor puts down to a condition I already had`
                            `the scarring is permanent`                     IS `m`'s `for scarring, it is permanent`
                            `the scarring was caused by burns claimed for the same part` IS `m`'s `for scarring, it was caused by burns I also claim for that part`) `mine`

GIVEN `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `I reported it to police within a reasonable time`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `I reported it to police before the decision`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was hurt while committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Section 43 facts`
`my s 43 facts` `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled` `I reported it to police within a reasonable time` `I reported it to police before the decision` `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report` `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way` `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender` `I was hurt while committing an indictable offence` MEANS
    `Section 43 facts` WITH
        `the assessor is satisfied the applicant is not entitled to an award` IS `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled`
        `the act was reported to a police officer within a reasonable time`  IS `I reported it to police within a reasonable time`
        `the act was reported to a police officer before the decision`       IS `I reported it to police before the decision`
        `the assessor is satisfied circumstances prevented the report`       IS `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report`
        `the applicant failed without reasonable excuse to assist police in a material way` IS `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way`
        `the assessor is satisfied the application was made in collusion with the offender` IS `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender`
        `the injury or death occurred while the applicant was committing an indictable offence` IS `I was hurt while committing an indictable offence`

§§ `ss 5-7, regs 4-7, 15 and Schedules 1-2 -- the violent act and the injury`

@export Is what happened to me a "violent act" under the Victims of Crime Assistance Act (NT) (s 5, reg 4)?
GIVEN `it happened in the Northern Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the criminal act happened in the Northern Territory (the injury or death can have happened anywhere)
      `it was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a criminal offence, or would have been one if the offender had not been excused by age, mental impairment, other legal incapacity or another lawful defence (an attempt counts, s 5(7))
      `it directly caused someone's injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it directly caused anyone's injury (a physical injury or illness, a recognised psychological or psychiatric disorder, or pregnancy) or death
      `the Criminal Code section of the offence` IS A STRING @desc The NT Criminal Code section of the offence, written as the Regulations write it, for example 208H, 208HA, 208JI, 125D, 186B, 156, 189, 196; for an offence before 25 March 2024 the old number, such as 127(1)(a), 130(3A)(b), 131A, 188, 192(3), 192B; for an attempt, the section attempted
      `it was an attempt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was an attempt to commit the offence in that section
      `the date of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The date the offence was committed (it decides whether the Schedules' rows for the Code before 25 March 2024 or before 30 April 2023 apply)
      `the victim suffered serious harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim suffered serious harm (Criminal Code meaning) as a direct result of the offence (a factor of aggravation, reg 7(a))
      `an offensive weapon was used or threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was committed by the use or threatened use of an offensive weapon (reg 7(b))
      `the offender was in the company of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offender committed it in the company of another person (reg 7(c))
      `old s 188(2)(a) applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for an assault under old s 188 (before 25 March 2024): whether the circumstance in s 188(2)(a) applied; otherwise no
      `old s 188(2)(c) applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for an assault under old s 188: whether the circumstance in s 188(2)(c) applied; otherwise no
      `old s 188(2)(k) applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for an assault under old s 188: whether the circumstance in s 188(2)(k) applied; otherwise no
      `the Schedule 2 condition for the offence applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For s 196, whether it was committed on an unlawful entry of a building; for s 218, whether in a circumstance in s 219(1); for old s 211(1), whether in a circumstance in s 211(2); otherwise no
      `how many related criminal acts there were` IS A NUMBER @desc How many related criminal acts the violent act is made up of (1 for a single act; a series against you at about the same time, or over time by the same people, counts as one violent act, s 5(3)-(4))
      `the acts happened over a period of time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the related acts happened over a period of time rather than all at once
      `the acts were all by the same offender against the same victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all the related acts were committed by the same offender against the same victim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a violent act` IF
    `is a violent act` (`the act from my answers` `it happened in the Northern Territory` `it was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` `it directly caused someone's injury or death` (`the offence from my answers` `the Criminal Code section of the offence` `it was an attempt` `the date of the offence` `the victim suffered serious harm` `an offensive weapon was used or threatened` `the offender was in the company of another person` `old s 188(2)(a) applied` `old s 188(2)(c) applied` `old s 188(2)(k) applied` `the Schedule 2 condition for the offence applied` `how many related criminal acts there were` `the acts happened over a period of time` `the acts were all by the same offender against the same victim`))

@export Is it a compensable violent act, and if so what is its category (1 to 4) and its standard amount (s 7(1), regs 4, 14, Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `it happened in the Northern Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the criminal act happened in the Northern Territory
      `it was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a criminal offence, or would have been but for age, mental impairment, other incapacity or a lawful defence
      `it directly caused someone's injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it directly caused anyone's injury or death
      `the Criminal Code section of the offence` IS A STRING @desc The NT Criminal Code section, as the Regulations write it (for example 208H, 208AB, 208JI, 186B; before 25 March 2024, 127(1)(a), 192(3), 192B, 131A); for an attempt, the section attempted
      `it was an attempt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was an attempt
      `the date of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The date the offence was committed
      `the victim suffered serious harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim suffered serious harm as a direct result (reg 7(a))
      `an offensive weapon was used or threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an offensive weapon was used or threatened (reg 7(b))
      `the offender was in the company of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offender was in the company of another person (reg 7(c))
      `old s 188(2)(a) applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for old s 188: whether s 188(2)(a) applied; otherwise no
      `old s 188(2)(c) applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for old s 188: whether s 188(2)(c) applied; otherwise no
      `old s 188(2)(k) applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for old s 188: whether s 188(2)(k) applied; otherwise no
      `the Schedule 2 condition for the offence applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for ss 196, 218 and old s 211(1): whether the condition opposite in Schedule 2 applied; otherwise no
      `how many related criminal acts there were` IS A NUMBER @desc How many related criminal acts make up the violent act (a pattern of abuse needs 3 or more, reg 6)
      `the acts happened over a period of time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the related acts happened over a period of time
      `the acts were all by the same offender against the same victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they were all by the same offender against the same victim
GIVETH A `Compensable violent act answer`
DECIDE `What category of compensable violent act is it` IS
    `the s 7(1) answer for` (`the act from my answers` `it happened in the Northern Territory` `it was a criminal offence, or would have been but for an excuse` `it directly caused someone's injury or death` (`the offence from my answers` `the Criminal Code section of the offence` `it was an attempt` `the date of the offence` `the victim suffered serious harm` `an offensive weapon was used or threatened` `the offender was in the company of another person` `old s 188(2)(a) applied` `old s 188(2)(c) applied` `old s 188(2)(k) applied` `the Schedule 2 condition for the offence applied` `how many related criminal acts there were` `the acts happened over a period of time` `the acts were all by the same offender against the same victim`))

@export Is the harm I suffered an "injury" under the Act (s 6)?
GIVEN `I have a physical illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a physical illness or injury
      `I have a recognised psychological or psychiatric disorder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a recognisable psychological or psychiatric disorder (diagnosed, not ordinary distress)
      `I became pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became pregnant as a result
      `it comes from losing property or property damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harm results from the loss of, or damage to, property (that is not an injury, s 6(2))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my harm an injury` IF
    `is an injury` `I have a physical illness or injury` `I have a recognised psychological or psychiatric disorder` `I became pregnant` `it comes from losing property or property damage`

@export Did I suffer "domestic violence injuries" (reg 5), which have their own standard amount of $10 000?
GIVEN `I was injured as a direct result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered at least one injury as a direct result of the violent act
      `it was a pattern of abuse by someone I am in a domestic relationship with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act involved a pattern of abuse (3 or more related criminal acts over time by the same offender against you) committed by someone you are in a domestic relationship with (Domestic and Family Violence Act 2007 meaning)
      `it was stalking in breach of a domestic violence order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was unlawful stalking (Criminal Code s 189) in contravention, or apparent contravention, of a domestic violence order
      `it was a combination of those by the same offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a combination of those acts by the same offender
      `the injuries are more than transient or trifling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injuries are more than transient or trifling (they need not be serious)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I suffer domestic violence injuries` IF
    `suffers domestic violence injuries` `I was injured as a direct result` `it was a pattern of abuse by someone I am in a domestic relationship with` `it was stalking in breach of a domestic violence order` `it was a combination of those by the same offender` `the injuries are more than transient or trifling`

DECLARE `Disorder item answer` IS ONE OF
    `my disorder is Schedule 3 item` HAS `item` IS A STRING
    `my disorder has no Schedule 3 item 12 amount (reg 15: it must be chronic, at least moderately disabling, from a Schedule 1 or 2 offence or, if severely disabling, from domestic violence injuries, and last more than 13 weeks)`

@export Which Schedule 3 item is my psychological or psychiatric disorder, if any (reg 15, Schedule 3 item 12)?
GIVEN `how disabling it is` IS A `How disabling` @desc How disabling the disorder is: mildly or not disabling, moderately disabling, or severely disabling (a clinical assessment)
      `it is chronic` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disorder is chronic
      `the offence is in Schedule 1 or 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disorder results directly from an offence listed in Schedule 1 or Schedule 2 of the Regulations, with its condition (the compensable violent act question answers Schedule 1)
      `it comes from domestic violence injuries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it results from a violent act causing domestic violence injuries (see the domestic violence injuries question)
      `how many weeks it has lasted or will last` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks the disorder has lasted, or is expected to last
      `it is permanent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disorder is permanent
GIVETH A `Disorder item answer`
DECIDE `Which Schedule 3 item is my disorder` IS
    CONSIDER `the item 12 leaf for` (`the reg 15 category of the disorder` `how disabling it is` `it is chronic` `the offence is in Schedule 1 or 2` `it comes from domestic violence injuries`) `how many weeks it has lasted or will last` `it is permanent`
    WHEN JUST `item` THEN `my disorder is Schedule 3 item` `item`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `my disorder has no Schedule 3 item 12 amount (reg 15: it must be chronic, at least moderately disabling, from a Schedule 1 or 2 offence or, if severely disabling, from domestic violence injuries, and last more than 13 weeks)`

§§ `ss 9-16, 22 -- what kind of victim I am, and what I may apply for`

@export Which kinds of victim of the violent act am I: primary, secondary, family or related (ss 9, 11, 13, 15)?
GIVEN `it is a violent act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what happened is a violent act (see the violent act question)
      `it is a compensable violent act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a compensable violent act, a Schedule 1 sexual offence (see the compensable violent act question)
      `it was committed against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act was committed against you
      `I was injured as a direct result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered an injury (physical, a recognised psychological or psychiatric disorder, or pregnancy) as a direct result of it
      `I was injured trying to stop it, help a victim or arrest the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured trying to prevent the violent act, to help or rescue someone it was committed against, or to arrest the person committing it
      `I was there and was injured by witnessing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were present at the scene and suffered an injury as a direct result of witnessing it
      `I was injured on later learning of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered an injury as a direct result of becoming aware of it afterwards
      `I am the primary victim's child, stepchild or child in their care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a child or stepchild of the person it was committed against, or a child under their guardianship (including a child born after it)
      `I am the primary victim's parent, step-parent or guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a parent, step-parent or guardian of the person it was committed against
      `the primary victim was a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person it was committed against was under 18 when it happened
      `I am the primary victim's spouse or de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the spouse or de facto partner of the person it was committed against
      `I depended on the primary victim financially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entirely or substantially dependent on the person it was committed against for financial support
      `I am a relative of the primary victim or in an intimate relationship with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a relative of the person it was committed against, or in an intimate personal relationship with them
      `I committed the violent act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you committed the violent act (then you are not a secondary, family or related victim)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Category of victim`
DECIDE `Which kinds of victim am I` IS
    `the categories of`
        (`Person and the violent act` WITH
            `the act is a violent act`                                                   IS `it is a violent act`
            `the act is a compensable violent act`                                       IS `it is a compensable violent act`
            `the act was committed against the person`                                   IS `it was committed against me`
            `the person suffered an injury as a direct result`                           IS `I was injured as a direct result`
            -- placeholder: a person asking for themselves is alive; s 9's "or dies" is read in the funeral seat
            `the person died as a direct result`                                         IS FALSE
            `the person was injured or died trying to prevent the act, help or rescue a victim, or arrest the offender` IS `I was injured trying to stop it, help a victim or arrest the offender`
            `the person was present at the scene and was injured as a direct result of witnessing the act` IS `I was there and was injured by witnessing it`
            `the person was injured as a direct result of later becoming aware of the act` IS `I was injured on later learning of it`
            `the person is a child or stepchild of the primary victim, or a child under their guardianship` IS `I am the primary victim's child, stepchild or child in their care`
            `the person is a parent, step-parent or guardian of the primary victim`      IS `I am the primary victim's parent, step-parent or guardian`
            `the primary victim was a child when the act occurred`                       IS `the primary victim was a child`
            `the person is the spouse or de facto partner of the primary victim`         IS `I am the primary victim's spouse or de facto partner`
            `the person was entirely or substantially dependent on the primary victim for financial support` IS `I depended on the primary victim financially`
            `the person is a relative of the primary victim, or in an intimate personal relationship with them` IS `I am a relative of the primary victim or in an intimate relationship with them`
            `the person committed the violent act`                                       IS `I committed the violent act`)

-- The facts for ss 17-18, from plain answers.
GIVEN `the injured person is or was paid a motor accidents benefit for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person is entitled to a motor accidents benefit for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person is a worker under the Return to Work Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person is or was paid return to work compensation for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person is entitled to return to work compensation for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return to work claim is disputed and undecided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Other scheme facts`
`the other scheme facts from my answers` `the injured person is or was paid a motor accidents benefit for the injury` `the injured person is entitled to a motor accidents benefit for it` `the injured person is a worker under the Return to Work Act` `the injured person is or was paid return to work compensation for it` `the injured person is entitled to return to work compensation for it` `the return to work claim is disputed and undecided` MEANS
    `Other scheme facts` WITH
        `the injured person is being paid, or has been paid, a Motor Accidents (Compensation) benefit for the injury` IS `the injured person is or was paid a motor accidents benefit for the injury`
        `the injured person is entitled to a Motor Accidents (Compensation) benefit for the injury, claimed or not` IS `the injured person is entitled to a motor accidents benefit for it`
        `the injured person is a worker under the Return to Work Act 1986`        IS `the injured person is a worker under the Return to Work Act`
        `the worker is being paid, or has been paid, Return to Work compensation for the injury` IS `the injured person is or was paid return to work compensation for it`
        `the worker is entitled to Return to Work compensation for the injury, claimed or not` IS `the injured person is entitled to return to work compensation for it`
        `the worker's claim is disputed, referred to mediation or a proceeding, and undetermined` IS `the return to work claim is disputed and undecided`

@export What may I apply for: counselling, an interim payment, an award for financial loss, for the compensable violent act, or for compensable injuries (ss 10, 12, 14, 16, 17, 18, 22, 25, 26)?
GIVEN `the kind of victim I apply as` IS A `Category of victim` @desc The one category you apply in (s 25(1)): primary victim, secondary victim, family victim or related victim (see the kinds of victim question)
      `it is a compensable violent act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act is a compensable violent act (see that question)
      `I have a compensable injury from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have at least one injury listed in Schedule 3 of the Regulations, or similar to one, from the violent act
      `I am in financial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in circumstances of financial hardship (the Director decides; answer as you expect)
      `the primary victim died from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act directly resulted in the death of the person it was committed against
      `the injured person is or was paid a motor accidents benefit for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person (you, if you are the primary victim) is being or has been paid a benefit under the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 for the injury
      `the injured person is entitled to a motor accidents benefit for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is entitled to a Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act benefit for the injury, whether or not they claimed it
      `the injured person is a worker under the Return to Work Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is a worker as the Return to Work Act 1986 defines it, injured at work
      `the injured person is or was paid return to work compensation for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is being or has been paid compensation under the Return to Work Act 1986 for the injury
      `the injured person is entitled to return to work compensation for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is entitled to Return to Work Act compensation for the injury, whether or not they claimed it
      `the return to work claim is disputed and undecided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person claimed under the Return to Work Act, the employer disputed liability, the dispute went to mediation or a proceeding, and it is not yet decided
      `I have already applied for an award for this act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already applied for an award for this violent act (only one award application per act, s 25(2))
      `my award application has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor has already decided your application for an award (no interim payment after that, s 26(2A))
      `interim payments I have already had` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of interim payments already paid to you for this act, in Australian dollars (at most $5 000 in all)
GIVETH A `What may be applied for`
DECIDE `What may I apply for` IS
    `what may be applied for in`
        (`Application position` WITH
            `the category applied in`                                  IS `the kind of victim I apply as`
            `the act is a compensable violent act`                     IS `it is a compensable violent act`
            `has one or more compensable injuries from the act`        IS `I have a compensable injury from it`
            `is in circumstances of financial hardship`                IS `I am in financial hardship`
            `the act directly resulted in the death of the primary victim` IS `the primary victim died from it`
            `excluded by s 17 or s 18`                                 IS `excludes an interim payment or award` (`the s 17 and 18 answer for` (`the other scheme facts from my answers` `the injured person is or was paid a motor accidents benefit for the injury` `the injured person is entitled to a motor accidents benefit for it` `the injured person is a worker under the Return to Work Act` `the injured person is or was paid return to work compensation for it` `the injured person is entitled to return to work compensation for it` `the return to work claim is disputed and undecided`) (`the kind of victim I apply as` EQUALS `primary victim`))
            `has already applied for an award for the same violent act` IS `I have already applied for an award for this act`
            `the assessor has decided the application for an award`   IS `my award application has been decided`
            `interim payments already paid for the act`                IS `interim payments I have already had`)

§§ `ss 17-18 and reg 13 -- injured at work or on the road (asked only if a motor accident or work injury is involved)`

@export Does a motor accidents (compensation) or return to work entitlement stop me getting an interim payment or award (ss 17, 18, reg 13)?
GIVEN `I am the injured person, claiming for that injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Yes if you are the person injured and claim as a primary victim for the same (or substantially the same) injury; no if you are a secondary or family victim of the act against the injured person
      `the injured person is or was paid a motor accidents benefit for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is being or has been paid a benefit under the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 for the injury
      `the injured person is entitled to a motor accidents benefit for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is entitled to such a benefit, whether or not they claimed it (see the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act encoding)
      `the injured person is a worker under the Return to Work Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is a worker under the Return to Work Act 1986
      `the injured person is or was paid return to work compensation for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is being or has been paid Return to Work Act compensation for the injury
      `the injured person is entitled to return to work compensation for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is entitled to Return to Work Act compensation for it, whether or not they claimed it (see the Return to Work Act encoding)
      `the return to work claim is disputed and undecided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Return to Work claim was made, the employer disputed liability, the worker took it to mediation or a proceeding, and it is not yet decided
GIVETH AN `Other scheme answer`
DECIDE `Does another scheme stop my claim` IS
    `the s 17 and 18 answer for` (`the other scheme facts from my answers` `the injured person is or was paid a motor accidents benefit for the injury` `the injured person is entitled to a motor accidents benefit for it` `the injured person is a worker under the Return to Work Act` `the injured person is or was paid return to work compensation for it` `the injured person is entitled to return to work compensation for it` `the return to work claim is disputed and undecided`) `I am the injured person, claiming for that injury`

§§ `ss 25-28 -- interim payment (asked only if I am in financial hardship)`

@export Can I apply for an interim payment for my financial loss, and for how much at most (ss 10(2), 12(2), 14(2), 25(3), 26, 27(5))?
GIVEN `the kind of victim I apply as` IS A `Category of victim` @desc The one category you apply in: primary victim, secondary victim, family victim or related victim
      `I am in financial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in circumstances of financial hardship
      `the primary victim died from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act directly resulted in the death of the person it was committed against (needed for a family victim)
      `excluded by ss 17-18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accidents and return to work question says you are excluded
      `my award application has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor has already decided your application for an award
      `interim payments I have already had` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of interim payments already paid to you for this act, in Australian dollars
      `the financial loss I need it for` IS A NUMBER @desc The financial loss the interim payment is for, in Australian dollars (lost earnings, medical expenses, lost clothing or personal effects, or in exceptional cases other recovery costs)
GIVETH AN `Interim answer`
DECIDE `How much interim payment can I apply for` IS
    `the interim payment answer for` `my position` `the financial loss I need it for`
    WHERE
        `my position` MEANS
                `Application position` WITH
                    `the category applied in`                                  IS `the kind of victim I apply as`
                    -- placeholders: these three fields are read only for awards, not for an interim payment
                    `the act is a compensable violent act`                     IS FALSE
                    `has one or more compensable injuries from the act`        IS FALSE
                    `has already applied for an award for the same violent act` IS FALSE
                    `is in circumstances of financial hardship`                IS `I am in financial hardship`
                    `the act directly resulted in the death of the primary victim` IS `the primary victim died from it`
                    `excluded by s 17 or s 18`                                 IS `excluded by ss 17-18`
                    `the assessor has decided the application for an award`   IS `my award application has been decided`
                    `interim payments already paid for the act`                IS `interim payments I have already had`

§§ `regs 16, 18-23 and ss 38(3), 39(3) -- standard amounts and loss of earnings`

@export What is the standard amount that may be awarded for my compensable injuries, after the multiple-injury and existing-condition rules (regs 16, 18-22, Schedule 3)?
GIVEN `my injuries` IS A LIST OF `My injury` @desc Each injury from the violent act: its Schedule 3, Part 2 item down to the leaf (for example 6.7(a), 1.2(a)(ii), 12(b)(i), or 4 for domestic violence injuries; for an unlisted injury, the most similar listed item); whether it is on both sides of your body or to your only remaining eye, ear, arm or other part; the percent the assessor attributes to a condition you already had (0 if none); and, for scarring, whether it is permanent and whether it was caused by burns you also claim for that part
GIVETH AN `Injury amount answer`
DECIDE `What is the standard amount for my injuries` IS
    `the standard amount for the injuries` (`my injuries as claimed` `my injuries`)

DECLARE `Threshold answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the standard amounts total at least $7 500` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no: the standard amounts total less than $7 500, so no award for the injuries (financial loss can still be awarded)` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: an item is not a leaf of Schedule 3, Part 2` HAS `the item` IS A STRING

@export Do my compensable injuries reach the $7 500 an award for injuries needs (ss 38(3), 39(3))?
GIVEN `my injuries` IS A LIST OF `My injury` @desc Each injury from the violent act, as in the standard amount question
GIVETH A `Threshold answer`
DECIDE `Do my injuries reach the threshold` IS
    CONSIDER `the first item not in Schedule 3` (`my injuries as claimed` `my injuries`)
    WHEN JUST `bad` THEN `not covered: an item is not a leaf of Schedule 3, Part 2` `bad`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the injuries reach the s 38(3) threshold` (`my injuries as claimed` `my injuries`)
        THEN `yes: the standard amounts total at least $7 500` (`the total of the standard amounts for the threshold` (`my injuries as claimed` `my injuries`))
        ELSE `no: the standard amounts total less than $7 500, so no award for the injuries (financial loss can still be awarded)` (`the total of the standard amounts for the threshold` (`my injuries as claimed` `my injuries`))

@export How much loss of earnings can be assessed for me (reg 23)?
GIVEN `the kind of victim I apply as` IS A `Category of victim` @desc The category you apply in: primary victim, secondary victim, family victim or related victim
      `NT average weekly earnings less notional tax` IS A NUMBER @desc The ABS Average Weekly Earnings, full-time adult ordinary time, for the Northern Territory, last published before the calculation, less a notional deduction for income tax, in Australian dollars a week (not in the deposited texts: give the figure)
      `my net weekly earnings when it happened` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net (after tax) weekly earnings at the date of the violent act, in Australian dollars
      `my net weekly earnings during the period` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net weekly earnings during the period of lost earnings, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `how many weeks I lost earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks the loss of earnings lasted or is likely to last
GIVETH A `Loss of earnings answer`
DECIDE `How much loss of earnings can be assessed` IS
    `the reg 23 answer for` `the kind of victim I apply as` `NT average weekly earnings less notional tax` `my net weekly earnings when it happened` `my net weekly earnings during the period` `how many weeks I lost earnings`

§§ `ss 37-43 -- the award`

@export As a primary victim, what is the most I can be awarded, after the caps, the s 41 and s 42 reductions and the s 43 bars (ss 10, 37, 38, 41-43)?
GIVEN `I am a primary victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a primary victim of the violent act (see the kinds of victim question)
      `excluded by ss 17-18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accidents and return to work question says you are excluded for this injury
      `what my award is for` IS A `What the award is for` @desc What you apply for: your financial loss only; the mere commission of a compensable violent act with your financial loss; or your compensable injuries with your financial loss (s 10(4): the act or the injuries, not both)
      `the category of the compensable violent act` IS A NUMBER @desc The category of the compensable violent act, 1 to 4, from the compensable violent act question (0 if it is not one)
      `my injuries` IS A LIST OF `My injury` @desc Each injury from the violent act, as in the standard amount question (an empty list if you claim none)
      `my lost earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your loss of earnings from the violent act, in Australian dollars (see the loss of earnings question)
      `my lost clothing and personal effects` IS A NUMBER @desc What you spent because clothing and other personal effects were lost as a direct result, in Australian dollars
      `my medical expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Medical, dental, psychological, ambulance, hospital and physiotherapy expenses and medical reports reasonably incurred or likely, in Australian dollars
      `my other recovery expenses in exceptional circumstances` IS A NUMBER @desc In exceptional circumstances only, other expenses reasonably incurred to help you recover (such as relocating or securing your home), in Australian dollars; otherwise 0
      `interim payments I received` IS A NUMBER @desc The interim payments you received for this violent act, in Australian dollars
      `the s 41 reduction the assessor makes` IS A NUMBER @desc Any reduction the assessor considers reasonable for your own conduct, failure to mitigate, or benefit to the offender (s 41), in Australian dollars; 0 if none
      `payments I received for the same act, injury or loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Payments you received for the same act, injury or loss: damages or compensation from the offender, private health insurance, a benefit or compensation under any Australian Act (such as motor accidents or workers compensation), insurance or agreement payments, or an interim payment you were not entitled to (s 42), in Australian dollars
      `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied you are not entitled to an award (s 43(a))
      `I reported it to police within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act was reported to a police officer within a reasonable time after it happened
      `I reported it to police before the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act was reported to a police officer before the assessor decides
      `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied circumstances prevented the report being made
      `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed, without reasonable excuse, to assist police in a material way, including by not making a formal complaint or statement
      `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied you made the application in collusion with the offender
      `I was hurt while committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury occurred while you were committing an indictable offence
GIVETH AN `Award answer`
DECIDE `How much can I be awarded as a primary victim` IS
    `the award to a primary victim` `I am a primary victim` `excluded by ss 17-18` `what my award is for` `the category of the compensable violent act` (`my injuries as claimed` `my injuries`) (`the s 10(5) financial loss` `my lost earnings` `my lost clothing and personal effects` `my medical expenses` `my other recovery expenses in exceptional circumstances`) `interim payments I received` (`my s 43 facts` `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled` `I reported it to police within a reasonable time` `I reported it to police before the decision` `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report` `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way` `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender` `I was hurt while committing an indictable offence`) `the s 41 reduction the assessor makes` `payments I received for the same act, injury or loss`

@export As a secondary victim, what is the most I can be awarded, sharing the $40 000 with the other secondary victims, after the reductions and bars (ss 12, 37, 39, 41-43)?
GIVEN `I am a secondary victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a secondary victim of the violent act (see the kinds of victim question)
      `excluded by ss 17-18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accidents and return to work question says you are excluded (as a secondary victim of an act against someone those Acts cover)
      `my injuries` IS A LIST OF `My injury` @desc Each injury you suffered from witnessing or learning of the act, as in the standard amount question (an empty list if none)
      `my lost earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your loss of earnings from witnessing or learning of the act, in Australian dollars
      `my medical expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Medical expenses reasonably incurred or likely, in Australian dollars
      `my other recovery expenses in exceptional circumstances` IS A NUMBER @desc In exceptional circumstances only, other recovery expenses (such as relocating), in Australian dollars; otherwise 0
      `interim payments I received` IS A NUMBER @desc The interim payments you received for this act, in Australian dollars
      `I saw the primary victim die at the scene and am their parent, guardian or child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you witnessed the primary victim's death at the scene and, at that time, were the parent or guardian of the primary victim (a child), or the primary victim's child or a child in their guardianship (s 39(5): these victims are awarded first)
      `the assessed total of the other secondary victims who saw the death` IS A NUMBER @desc The total assessed for the other secondary victims of this act who are in that priority group, in Australian dollars (0 if none or unknown)
      `the assessed total of the other secondary victims` IS A NUMBER @desc The total assessed for the other secondary victims of this act who are not in that group, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `interim payments to all secondary victims of the act` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of interim payments to all the secondary victims of this act, including yours, in Australian dollars
      `the s 41 reduction the assessor makes` IS A NUMBER @desc Any reduction the assessor considers reasonable under s 41, in Australian dollars; 0 if none
      `payments I received for the same act, injury or loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Payments received for the same injury or loss from the offender, insurance, or under any Australian Act (s 42), in Australian dollars
      `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied you are not entitled to an award (s 43(a))
      `I reported it to police within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act was reported to a police officer within a reasonable time
      `I reported it to police before the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was reported to a police officer before the assessor decides
      `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied circumstances prevented a report
      `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed, without reasonable excuse, to assist police in a material way
      `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied you applied in collusion with the offender
      `I was hurt while committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury occurred while you were committing an indictable offence
GIVETH AN `Award answer`
DECIDE `How much can I be awarded as a secondary victim` IS
    `the award to a secondary victim` `I am a secondary victim` `excluded by ss 17-18` (`my injuries as claimed` `my injuries`) (`the s 12(6) financial loss` `my lost earnings` `my medical expenses` `my other recovery expenses in exceptional circumstances`) `interim payments I received` `I saw the primary victim die at the scene and am their parent, guardian or child` `the assessed total of the other secondary victims who saw the death` `the assessed total of the other secondary victims` `interim payments to all secondary victims of the act` (`my s 43 facts` `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled` `I reported it to police within a reasonable time` `I reported it to police before the decision` `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report` `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way` `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender` `I was hurt while committing an indictable offence`) `the s 41 reduction the assessor makes` `payments I received for the same act, injury or loss`

@export As a family victim of someone killed by a violent act, what is the most I can be awarded, sharing the $40 000 with the other family victims, after the reductions and bars (ss 14, 37, 40-43)?
GIVEN `I am a family victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a family victim of the violent act (see the kinds of victim question)
      `the primary victim died from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act directly resulted in the primary victim's death (a family victim's award needs it)
      `excluded by ss 17-18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accidents and return to work question says you are excluded (as a family victim of an act against someone those Acts cover)
      `I depended on the primary victim financially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entirely or substantially dependent on the primary victim for financial support (dependants are awarded first, s 40(5))
      `the money I would have had from them in the year after the death` IS A NUMBER @desc Only if you were dependent: the money you would reasonably likely have received from the primary victim in the year after the death, in Australian dollars
      `medical expenses I had for the primary victim` IS A NUMBER @desc Medical expenses you reasonably incurred, or are likely to, for the primary victim as a direct result of the death, in Australian dollars
      `my other recovery expenses in exceptional circumstances` IS A NUMBER @desc In exceptional circumstances only, other expenses to help you recover from the death (such as relocating), in Australian dollars; otherwise 0
      `interim payments I received` IS A NUMBER @desc The interim payments you received for this act, in Australian dollars
      `the assessed total of the other dependent family victims` IS A NUMBER @desc The total assessed for the other family victims who were dependent on the primary victim, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `the assessed total of the other family victims` IS A NUMBER @desc The total assessed for the other family victims who were not dependent, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `interim payments to all family victims of the act` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of interim payments to all the family victims of this act, including yours, in Australian dollars
      `the assessor is satisfied no other family victim is likely to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied no other family victim of the act is likely to apply (s 40(8))
      `months since the latest family victim application` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months have passed since the latest application by a family victim of this act
      `another family victim has applied or said they will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another family victim has applied, or told the assessor they intend to, since then
      `the s 41 reduction the assessor makes` IS A NUMBER @desc Any reduction the assessor considers reasonable under s 41, in Australian dollars; 0 if none
      `payments I received for the same death or loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Payments you received for the same death or loss from the offender, insurance, or under any Australian Act (for example a motor accidents or workers compensation death benefit), in Australian dollars (s 42)
      `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied you are not entitled to an award (s 43(a))
      `it was reported to police within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act was reported to a police officer within a reasonable time
      `it was reported to police before the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was reported to a police officer before the assessor decides
      `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied circumstances prevented a report
      `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed, without reasonable excuse, to assist police in a material way
      `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied you applied in collusion with the offender
      `the death occurred while I was committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death occurred during the commission of an indictable offence by you (s 43(f))
GIVETH AN `Award answer`
DECIDE `How much can I be awarded as a family victim` IS
    `the award to a family victim` `I am a family victim` `the primary victim died from it` `excluded by ss 17-18` `I depended on the primary victim financially` (`the s 14(3) financial loss` `I depended on the primary victim financially` `the money I would have had from them in the year after the death` `medical expenses I had for the primary victim` `my other recovery expenses in exceptional circumstances`) `interim payments I received` `the assessed total of the other dependent family victims` `the assessed total of the other family victims` `interim payments to all family victims of the act` `the assessor is satisfied no other family victim is likely to apply` `months since the latest family victim application` `another family victim has applied or said they will` (`my s 43 facts` `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled` `it was reported to police within a reasonable time` `it was reported to police before the decision` `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report` `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way` `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender` `the death occurred while I was committing an indictable offence`) `the s 41 reduction the assessor makes` `payments I received for the same death or loss`

DECLARE `Bar answer` IS ONE OF
    `the assessor must refuse an award` HAS `because` IS A `Why no award`
    `s 43 does not bar an award`

@export Must the assessor refuse to make me an award because of how the act was reported, my cooperation with police, collusion, or my own offence (s 43)?
GIVEN `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied you are not entitled to an award (s 43(a))
      `I reported it to police within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the violent act was reported to a police officer within a reasonable time after it happened
      `I reported it to police before the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was reported to a police officer before the assessor decides
      `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied circumstances prevented the report being made
      `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed, without reasonable excuse, to assist police in a material way, including by not making a formal complaint or statement
      `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied you made the application in collusion with the offender
      `I was hurt while committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury or death occurred while you were committing an indictable offence
GIVETH A `Bar answer`
DECIDE `Must the assessor refuse an award` IS
    CONSIDER `the s 43 bar for` (`my s 43 facts` `the assessor is satisfied I am not entitled` `I reported it to police within a reasonable time` `I reported it to police before the decision` `the assessor is satisfied something prevented a report` `I failed without reasonable excuse to help police in a material way` `the assessor is satisfied I colluded with the offender` `I was hurt while committing an indictable offence`)
    WHEN JUST `why` THEN `the assessor must refuse an award` `why`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 43 does not bar an award`

§§ `ss 29, 45-47 -- payment, increase and refund (asked once a payment is approved or a refund is required)`

@export Within how many days after the approval or notice must the Territory pay me (ss 29, 45, 46(10))?
GIVEN `what is being paid` IS A `Payment of financial assistance` @desc What is being paid: an interim payment (counted from the Director's approval), an award or an increased award (counted from the Director's notice to you)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I be paid` IS
    `the days the Territory has to pay` `what is being paid`

@export By what date must I apply for an increased award (s 46(1))?
GIVEN `the date my award was paid` IS A DATE @desc The date the award was paid to you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (a child at the date of payment has 3 years after turning 18)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply for an increase` IS
    `the last day to apply for an increased award` `the date my award was paid` `my date of birth`

@export Can my award be increased (s 46(1), (5))?
GIVEN `the date my award was paid` IS A DATE @desc The date the award was paid to you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date I apply for the increase` IS A DATE @desc The date you apply to the Director for the increased award
      `the assessor is satisfied the circumstances require it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor is satisfied the circumstances require an increase (for example a worse injury or further loss)
      `the maximum has already been awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relevant maximum in s 38, 39 or 40 has already been awarded (for a primary victim, $40 000 less interim payments; for secondary or family victims, the shared maximum for the act)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my award be increased` IF
    `the award may be increased` (`the application for an increased award is in time` `the date my award was paid` `my date of birth` `the date I apply for the increase`) `the assessor is satisfied the circumstances require it` `the maximum has already been awarded`

@export If the assessor requires me to refund an award or interim payment, how many days do I have after I receive the notice, before it is overdue as a debt to the Territory (s 47)?
GIVEN `the days the notice gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the refund notice gives you, counted from when you receive it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How long do I have to refund` IS
    `the days to refund` `the days the notice gives me`

§§ `ss 47H-47K -- if CVSU could not contact me (asked only if a closure notice was sent)`

@export My application was, or may be, closed because I could not be contacted: is it open, closed, or must it be reopened (ss 47H-47K)?
GIVEN `a closure notice was sent to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a CVSU officer sent you a notice of proposed closure after failing to contact you for at least 3 months
      `I gave updated contact details within 30 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave a CVSU officer updated contact details within 30 days after the date of the notice
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the notice of proposed closure
      `I asked the Director to reopen it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have asked the Director to reopen the closed application
      `the date I asked, or today` IS A DATE @desc The date you asked the Director to reopen it, or today's date if you have not asked
GIVETH A `Closure answer`
DECIDE `Is my application open or closed` IS
    `the ss 47H-47K answer for` `a closure notice was sent to me` `I gave updated contact details within 30 days` `the date of the notice` `I asked the Director to reopen it` `the date I asked, or today`

§§ `s 48 and Schedule 1 -- review by NTCAT (asked once a decision is made)`

@export Can I apply to NTCAT for review of a decision on my application (s 48, Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision` @desc The decision: an assessor's decision on your award application (s 34), on an increased award (s 46(4)), or requiring a refund (s 47(1)); the Director's decision on funeral expense assistance (s 47E) or requiring its refund (s 47G(1)); the Director's interim payment decision (s 27); or the closure of your application (s 47J)
      `I am the applicant, or the person required to refund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the applicant for that decision (or, for a refund, the person required to refund)
      `days since I was given the decision` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since you were given the decision
      `days the NTCAT Act allows` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the Northern Territory Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2014 allows to apply for review (not in the deposited texts: give the figure)
GIVETH A `Review answer`
DECIDE `Can I apply for NTCAT review` IS
    `the s 48 answer for` `the decision` `I am the applicant, or the person required to refund` `days since I was given the decision` `days the NTCAT Act allows`

§§ `s 54 -- legal costs (asked only if a lawyer acts for me)`

@export What can my lawyer charge me for my application (s 54)?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN `Application kind` @desc The application the lawyer acts on: an interim payment (Division 2), an award (Division 3), an increased award (Division 5) or funeral expense assistance (Division 5A)
      `the reasonable disbursements charged` IS A NUMBER @desc The lawyer's reasonable disbursements (out-of-pocket expenses), in Australian dollars
      `counsel's fees in them` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of those disbursements is counsel's (a barrister's) fees, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A `Costs answer`
DECIDE `What can my lawyer charge me` IS
    `the s 54 answer for` `my application` `the reasonable disbursements charged` `counsel's fees in them`

§§ `s 19 -- if I die`

@export If I die, what happens to my eligibility or application, and does anything pass to my estate (s 19)?
GIVEN `when` IS A `Stage at death` @desc When the death would happen: before applying; after applying but before the application is decided; or after the assistance is approved or awarded but before it is paid
GIVETH A `Death answer`
DECIDE `What happens if I die` IS
    `the s 19 answer for` `when`
